From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:14:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: optical: en7570: use only the TGEN counters that were read

en7570_tgen() sweeps the T0/T1 timer reset points 32 times and keeps the
largest T0C and T1C it reads back, the limits of the upstream burst
timing. The result of each I2C read was ignored and the two-byte buffer
is not initialised: when a read failed, whatever the stack held went
into the maximum and from there into the timing registers of the laser
driver, and the function still returned 0.

Skip a sample whose read failed. If none could be read and the flash
holds no production values either, report it: the caller already stops
the GPON start when the timing calibration fails.

Found reading the code; no failed read has been seen on the XR500v.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/optical/airoha/en7570_txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/optical/airoha/en7570_txrx.c
@@ -329,6 +329,7 @@ int en7570_tgen(struct en7570_priv *priv
 	u32 t0ct1c = lddla_flash_read(&priv->lddla, EN7570_FL_T0CT1C);
 	u8 count[2];
 	u8 t0c = 0, t1c = 0;
+	int samples = 0;
 	u8 delay;
 	int i;
 
@@ -371,9 +372,12 @@ int en7570_tgen(struct en7570_priv *priv
 		lddla_update8(&priv->lddla, EN7570_T1DELAY + 3,
 			       EN7570_TGEN_METHOD2_MASK, 0);
 
-		lddla_rd(&priv->lddla, EN7570_T0C, count, sizeof(count));
+		/* a failed read leaves count as it was: do not take it */
+		if (lddla_rd(&priv->lddla, EN7570_T0C, count, sizeof(count)))
+			continue;
 		t0c = max(t0c, count[0]);
 		t1c = max(t1c, count[1]);
+		samples++;
 	}
 	mdelay(10);
 
@@ -407,6 +411,16 @@ int en7570_tgen(struct en7570_priv *priv
 
 	en7570_cdr(priv, true);			/* back to lock-to-data */
 	en7570_pattern_stop(priv);
+
+	/*
+	 * Without one counter from the sweep and without production values,
+	 * the burst timing above is not a measurement.
+	 */
+	if (!samples && t0ct1c == EN7570_FLASH_ERASED) {
+		dev_err(priv->lddla.dev,
+			"no TGEN counter could be read: burst timing not calibrated\n");
+		return -EIO;
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
